 MiniBang Guide

Welcome to MiniBang, a minimal Arch-based Xorg live ISO built around i3 for
low-RAM (~1GB) hardware.

Note: Do not post MiniBang issues on the Arch Linux forums.

---

PACMAN (LIVE SESSION)

Network required for pacman or browser use in the live session.

- Wired connections work automatically.
- Wireless: Super+n (nmtui), select network, enter password.

---

WORKSPACES

i3 uses numbered workspaces (1-9), tiling by default.

Switch workspaces with Super+1 through Super+9.
Toggle a window between floating and tiling with Super+Shift+Space.

---

POST-INSTALLATION

SUDO

Installed system requires password for sudo. Live session used passwordless sudo
for convenience — installed system does not.

---

INITIALIZE PACMAN

pacman will not work until keys are initialized:

fix-keys

This creates keys, refreshes the package cache, and updates archlinux-keyring.

---

BASIC PACKAGE USAGE

Search:   sudo pacman -Ss <package-name>
Install:  sudo pacman -S <package-name>

---

MICROCODE

MiniBang includes both intel-ucode and amd-ucode. You only need one.

If you remove the unused one after installation, update your bootloader config
(regenerate GRUB or edit loader.conf) before rebooting.

---

LIVE SESSION DISK SPACE

If the live session runs out of space:

sudo mount -o remount,size=8G /run/archiso/cowspace

